Block

The Operation: Operating at a steady-state
2,350 RPM (I4) or 1,950 RPM (V6), the

engine block features a nested micro-
triangular inner core, an intermediate offset

shear layer, and a macro-triangular outer
structural exoskeleton.
The Maintenance Breakthrough: The blocks
are completely unbonded. Four high-tensile
vertical steel tie-rods run from the cylinder

head down to the crankshaft bearings,
holding the entire stack in pure
compression. To swap a scratched cylinder
wall or a degraded Seebeck circuit, a
technician unbolts the four master tie-rods.
The Layer 1 Metallic Liner Pod or Layer 2
Thermal Seebeck Sleeve can be pulled
straight out like an ink cartridge from a
printer and swapped in under 20 minutes
without liquid sealants or gasket scrapers.

