Loop

The Operation: The exhaust gas enters a
stationary, 3D-printed aerodynamic nozzle.
Using the Coanda effect, the gas
automatically sways back and forth at
500\text{--}1,000\,\text{Hz} without a single
moving mechanical part.

The Electrical Capture: These high-frequency
pressure waves slam directly against
embedded Lead Zirconate Titanate (PZT)
piezoelectric crystal plates. The physical
compression generates a high-voltage
alternating current that easily clears the
400V+ threshold of the main traction battery,
requiring only a simple, rugged bridge
rectifier circuit to convert it to direct current.

Emissions Capture: Graded Gyroid Converter
Core

The Operation: The ionized plasma enters a
3D-printed, continuous Triply Periodic
Minimal Surface (TPMS) gyroid core infused
with a Coal Ash Zeolite metal catalyst. The
internal pathways shift seamlessly from 85%

porosity down to an ultra-dense 40% micro-
porous matrix along a smooth mathematical

gradient.
The Capture Output: Intense centripetal
